  "steps": [
    {
      "id": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000030d",
      "order": 0,
      "text": "Heat the oven to 200°C fan. Toss the sweet potato with 1 tbsp olive oil, the smoked paprika and salt; spread on a tray and roast for 20–25 minutes until caramelised at the edges."
    },
    {
      "id": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000030e",
      "order": 1,
      "text": "Meanwhile make the dressing: whisk the lemon juice, tahini, honey, garlic, remaining olive oil and cold water until smooth and pourable. Season with salt and pepper."
    },
    {
      "id": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000030f",
      "order": 2,
      "text": "Combine the chickpeas, spinach, cranberries and pumpkin seeds in a large bowl."
    },
    {
      "id": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000310",
      "order": 3,
      "text": "Fold in the roasted sweet potato while still warm so the spinach just wilts."
    },
    {
      "id": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000311",
      "order": 4,
      "text": "Pour over the dressing, toss well and top with the lemon zest and crumbled feta, if using."
    },
    {
      "id": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000312",
      "order": 5,
      "text": "Rest for 30 minutes before serving; it keeps, covered, in the fridge for 3 days."
    }
  ],
  "notesMarkdown": "## Why it works\n\nThe contrast of **soft roasted sweet potato**, **firm chickpeas** and **toasty seeds**\nmeans every forkful has texture. The dressing doubles as a dip.\n\n## Make ahead\n\nPrep everything up to step 4 a day ahead and keep the dressing separate;\ntoss just before serving so the salad stays crisp.\n\n## Add-ons\n\n- 100 g crumbled **crispy tofu** for extra protein.\n- A handful of **pomegranate seeds** instead of cranberries in season.\n\n> The tahini dressing thickens as it sits — loosen with a splash of water if needed.\n",
